#: ../../technical/topics/modelo-work-and-revision-lifecycle-part-1.md:26
msgid ""
"Input precedence is explicit: profile facts, source mesh, selected "
"Borrador 100 prefill, then admitted caller overrides. Profile binding "
"resolves date/enum/boolean/decimal channels under the pinned authority "
"and retains profile fingerprints; absent family or territory facts remain"
" unresolved. The Borrador route is opt-in by snapshot ID and accepts only"
" registry-marked AEAT-prefilled bindings. Work-review rows explain every "
"selected casilla's formula, realized source, provenance, blockers and "
"completeness role. Help cards render formula and dated parameters from "
"the same snapshot; they explain, but do not recalculate. Declarations "
"workspace/calendar project local and AEAT-evidence availability "
"separately, retaining stale/unreadable states and an unlinked AEAT "
"completion as distinct. Binding precedence "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/binding_resolution.py`) Profile binding "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/profile_binding.py`) Borrador selection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/borrador_binding.py`) Work review "
